About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

&nbsp;

Legal Counsel

Our Legal &amp; Business Integrity practice are looking for a Legal Counsel to join the team &nbsp;

Our Legal &amp; Business Integrity function partners with the business, providing specialized legal, commercial and risk management support, as well as sustainability advice, to enable confident growth. This spans everything from shaping and negotiating client and supplier contracts, to strategic partnerships, geographical expansion, insurance and company secretarial, restructuring, support for our corporate team (Baringa Enablement), and enterprise risk management. &nbsp;

Legal Counsel &nbsp;

Baringa is seeking a proactive, commercially minded Legal Counsel to join its Legal &amp; Business Integrity team. The role will support Baringa’s fast-growing North American business and may be performed remotely from anywhere in the United States or based in New York or Houston.

Baringa provides a broad range of management consulting services to clients primarily across the energy, telecommunications, government, and financial services sectors. &nbsp;

The successful candidate will be a self-starter and commercial transactions generalist who is comfortable taking ownership of matters from initial instruction through completion. They will be expected to work independently across a wide range of legal and commercial issues, exercise sound judgment, and provide practical, solutions-oriented advice. They must also recognize when a matter requires escalation or consultation with senior members of the Legal Team. &nbsp;

This role will play an important part in helping the Legal Team implement and embed Luminance, a new contract management and legal technology AI-enabled platform for the firm. The successful candidate should be comfortable adopting new technology, improving legal processes, and supporting consistent contracting practices across the business. &nbsp;

The Legal Counsel will work closely with stakeholders across Baringa and will report to the Senior Legal Counsel based in New York. &nbsp;

What you will be doing &nbsp;

• Drafting, reviewing, negotiating, and advising on a broad range of commercial agreements with clients, suppliers, partners, and other third parties. &nbsp;

• Taking primary responsibility for drafting, reviewing, and negotiating client engagement agreements, master services agreements, statements of work, licensing agreements, reliance letters, nondisclosure agreements, and related commercial d

Data Scientist, R.R. Donnelley & Sons Company, Warrenville, IL. Develop and implement a set of techniques or analytics applications to transform raw data into meaningful information using data-oriented programming languages and visualization software. Build and evaluate Marketing ML models using First & Third Party Customer Data. Create and manage end-to-end projects including analysis design, execution and summarization of results. Develop scalable data pipelines for feature extraction using various cloud services. Identify, clean, analyze and summarize data, potentially from disparate and complex data sources, to facilitate high quality analyses. Prototype and implement advance solutions to enhance existing ML model performance. Create clear documentation of research plans, results, and conclusions. Present research and recommendations based on research findings to audiences of varying level of experience. Collaborate with data engineering and operations teams to productionize work. Automate processes for recurring analyses or other model building activities, focusing on efficiency. Participate in planning, roadmap, and architecture discussions to help evolve our AI processes to improve revenue-generating products.
40 hrs/week, Mon-Fri, 8:30 a.m. - 5:30 p.m. Salary: $128,596.52 /yr. In addition to base salary, the total compensation package may also include participation in a bonus, commission or incentive program. RRD’s benefit offerings include medical, dental, and vision coverage, paid time off, disability insurance, 401(k) with company match, life insurance and other voluntary supplemental insurance coverages, plus parental leave, adoption assistance, tuition assistance and employer/partner discounts.
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS:
Master’s degree in Data Science, Computer Science or related field and two (2) years of experience in a computer occupation.
Must have two (2) years of experience with/in:

• Programming and sara analysis using Java, Python, Shell Scripting, PySpark, or SASSQL;

• Databases: PostgreSQL or MySQL;

• Data Visualization and Business Intelligence: Tableau, AWS QuickSight, Javascript, matplotlib, and seaborn;

• Big Data Analytics: Pentaho, Snowflake, AWS Redshift, or Hadoop;

• Cloud Computing: AWS (S3, RDS, SageMaker, Lambda, Step Functions, or Athena);

• Machine Learning Modeling: Supervised Learning, Unsupervised Learning, Feature Engineering, or Hyperparameter Tuning;

• Probability and Statistics;

• Agile Methodology;

• Version Control: Jenkins or Git;

• Data Exploration; and

• Data Visualization.

100% Telecommuting is permitted.
To apply, please submit your resume by visiting and searching the job code IL0219 - Data Scientist.
RRD is an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans
At RRD, we value innovation, authenticity, and integrity. To uphold the security and fairness of our hiring process, we ask that candidates refrain from using AI tools during interviews to ensure an authentic and secure experience. We appreciate your cooperation as we work to maintain a transparent and equitable hiring process.
All employment offers are contingent upon the successful completion of both a pre-employment background and drug screen.
RRD is a leading global provider of marketing, packaging, print, and supply chain solutions that elevate engagement across the complete customer journey. The company offers the industry’s most trusted portfolio of creative execution and world-wide business process consulting, with services designed to lower environmental impact. With 22,000 clients, including 93% of the Fortune 100, and 32,000 employees across 28 countries, RRD brings the expertise, execution, and scale designed to transform customer touchpoints into meaningful moments of impact.
